 the ctrl command's doing_dir check do? Currently `runCtrl` calls `SaveCtrlPrompt` which does the `doing directory not found` check. And the test says:\n> 异常（... ctrl doing 目录不存在）：... ctrl --dry-run --job job_N（doing 目录不存在）；操作 = 运行；预期 = ... ctrl 报 `doing directory not found` exit 非 0\n\nWait, the test says \"ctrl --dry-run --job job_N（doing 目录不存在）\" should report \"doing directory not found\". Let me check: currently `runCtrlDryRun` calls `SaveCtrlPrompt` which does the stat check and returns \"doing directory not found for job ...\". So this behavior must be preserved.\n\nAlso note: in `runCtrl` (non-dry-run), `SaveCtrlPrompt` also does the doing dir check. So both paths return \"doing directory not found\".\n\nBut wait, in the thin version, `Ctrl` handler should do the same. Let me preserve the exact error message: \"doing directory not found for job %s: %s\". The test just checks \"doing directory not found\" — so any message containing that substring works.\n\nNow, for the ctrl command, note the current `runCtrl` does NOT check `--job` before dry-run vs non-dry-run — both check GetJobID() first and return \"--job flag is required\". Good.\n\nNow let me think about the `Options` for these commands:\n- HumanLoop: needs topic, opts (Verbose, DryRun). No JobID needed. But the signature should probably be `HumanLoop(topic string, opts Options)`. The dry-run is handled in cli? No — looking at the current human_loop.go, the dry-run is handled inside the RunE. In the thin version, I should keep the dry-run branch in the cli (calling handler.HumanLoopDryRun) OR pass DryRun to handler.HumanLoop and let handler branch.\n\nLooking at the pattern from plan.go and doing.go:\n- plan.go: `if GetDryRun() { return handler.PlanDryRun() }` then `handler.Plan(requirement, opts)`.\n- doing.go: `if GetDryRun() { return handler.DoingDryRun(jobID) }` then `handler.Doing(jobID, opts)`.\n\nSo the pattern is: dry-run handled in cli via a separate handler function; non-dry-run via handler.Xxx with opts.\n\nFor human_loop.go, the current code has the dry-run branch INSIDE the RunE. I'll follow the plan/doing pattern:\n- cli: if GetDryRun() → handler.HumanLoopDryRun(topic); else handler.HumanLoop(topic, opts)\n\nBut wait, the current human_loop.go dry-run uses `pb.BuildHumanLoop` and prints content. There's no separate `HumanLoopDryRun` function currently. But the task says \"迁出 RunE 内编排 → handler.HumanLoop\". So I need to decide: does the dry-run logic go into handler.HumanLoop (with a DryRun branch) or a separate HumanLoopDryRun?\n\nThe task says: \"handler.HumanLoop：GetDraftDir → NextLoopID → 建目录 → builder.BuildHumanLoop（产 method+instance）→ env.Ensure → runtime.CallCLI（交互，注入 method）→ 持久化 sessionID\".\n\nHmm wait, this describes the non-dry-run flow. But it also says \"builder.BuildHumanLoop（产 method+instance）→ env.Ensure → runtime.CallCLI（交互，注入 method）→ 持久化 sessionID\". This is a new flow! Currently human-loop doesn't do env.Ensure or persist sessionID or inject method.\n\nWait, let me re-read the task goal:\n\n> 所有命令统一走「env.Ensure → builder.Build（产 method+instance 两份）→ 调用 runtime」编排；交互命令保留 `CallCLI`（行为不变，method 经 `--append-system-prompt` 传给 `CallCLI`），`runtime.Run` 结构化签名仅 task8 的 doing 使用。\n\nSo the unified orchestration is: env.Ensure → builder.Build (produce method+instance) → call runtime. Interactive commands keep CallCLI (behavior unchanged, method passed via --append-system-prompt to CallCLI). runtime.Run structured signature is only for task8's doing.\n\nSo for human-loop:\n- handler.HumanLoop: GetDraftDir → NextLoopID → mkdir → builder.BuildHumanLoop (method+instance) → env.Ensure → runtime.CallCLI (interactive, inject method via --append-system-prompt) → persist sessionID.\n\nHmm, but wait. The current human-loop flow uses `SaveHumanLoopPrompt` which returns mainFile, thinkFile, researchFile, exporterFile. The \"instance\" is the mainFile (sense_loop prompt file). And \"method\" is the commandMethod(\"human-loop\").\n\nAnd \"注入 method\" means passing method via `--append-system-prompt <methodFile>` to CallCLI. Let me check how runtime.CallCLI handles --append-system-prompt... CallCLI takes extraArgs which are appended before promptFile. So to inject method, I'd pass `\"--append-system-prompt\", methodFile` as extraArgs. But method is a string, not a file. Hmm.\n\nWait, let me look at how runtime.Run does it — it writes methodText to a temp file and passes `--append-system-prompt <methodFile>`. But CallCLI doesn't do that; CallCLI just takes extraArgs.\n\nSo for the handler to inject method via CallCLI, it needs to write the method text to a temp file first, then pass `--append-system-prompt <tempFile>` as extraArgs.\n\nHmm, but wait. Let me re-read the task goal again:\n\n> 交互命令保留 `CallCLI`（行为不变，method 经 `--append-system-prompt` 传给 `CallCLI`）\n\nSo method is passed via --append-system-prompt to CallCLI. This means the handler needs to write method to a temp file and pass `--append-system-prompt`, `<tempfile>` as extraArgs to CallCLI.\n\nBut hold on — does the existing task6 pattern (plan/doing/easy) do this? Let me check. Looking at handler/plan.go, it calls `runtime.CallCLI(opts.Verbose, cfg, planPromptFile, runtime.ModeInteractive)` — NO method injection! It uses `SavePlanPrompt` which returns promptFile and method, but then discards method and just calls CallCLI with the prompt file.\n\nWait, let me re-read handler/plan.go:\n\n```go\nplanPromptFile, _, err := builder.NewPIBuilder().SavePlanPrompt(requirement, jobPlanDir, rickDir)\n...\nif err := runtime.CallCLI(opts.Verbose, cfg, planPromptFile, runtime.ModeInteractive); err != nil {\n```\n\nSo it discards the method (`_`). Hmm. But the task goal says \"method 经 --append-system-prompt 传给 CallCLI\".\n\nWait, let me look more carefully at how task6 did it. The task6 commit says:\n> handler 不 import internal/cmd，flag 值经 Options{Verbose,DryRun,JobID} 在 cmd 调用点透传；本 task 中 doing 仍经 executor 执行，plan/easy 仍走 runtime.CallCLI 交互 TUI，runtime.Run 结构化签名 task8 再切换。\n\nSo in task6, plan/easy still use runtime.CallCLI interactive, but they don't inject method. Hmm. But the task7 goal says \"method 经 --append-system-prompt 传给 CallCLI\".\n\nWait, let me re-read the task7 goal once more:\n\n> 所有命令统一走「env.Ensure → builder.Build（产 method+instance 两份）→ 调用 runtime」编排；交互命令保留 `CallCLI`（行为不变，method 经 `--append-system-prompt` 传给 `CallCLI`），`runtime.Run` 结构化签名仅 task8 的 doing 使用。\n\nOK so this is the goal for task7. The key question: does \"env.Ensure\" already exist? Let me check the env package. And does the builder produce method+instance (which it does via BuildXxx returning method+instance)?\n\nLet me check the env package to understand `env.Ensure`.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider. The current plan/doing/easy handlers (task6) do NOT call env.Ensure. They call `workspace.New()` (which ensures dirs) and `config.LoadConfig()`. So does task7 require adding env.Ensure to the 4 new commands (human-loop/ctrl/dream/learning), or to ALL commands?\n\nThe task goal says \"所有命令统一走「env.Ensure → builder.Build（产 method+instance 两份）→ 调用 runtime」编排\". \"所有命令\" = all commands. But this is the GOAL statement. The actual per-command detail for human-loop says:\n\n> cli 保留 `NewHumanLoopCmd`（topic 校验：空则报「topic is required」）；迁出 RunE 内编排 → `handler.HumanLoop`：`GetDraftDir` → `NextLoopID` → 建目录 → `builder.BuildHumanLoop`（产 method+instance）→ `env.Ensure` → `runtime.CallCLI`（交互，注入 method）→ 持久化 sessionID\n\nSo handler.HumanLoop should: GetDraftDir → NextLoopID → mkdir → BuildHumanLoop (method+instance) → env.Ensure → CallCLI (inject method) → persist sessionID.\n\nThis is a NEW flow that differs from the current human_loop.go. The current flow uses `SaveHumanLoopPrompt` (which writes files). The new flow uses `BuildHumanLoop` (which returns method+instance strings without writing... wait, does BuildHumanLoop write the sense_loop prompt to a file?).\n\nLet me check. `BuildHumanLoop` calls `prompt.GenerateHumanLoopPrompt(topic, rfcDir, draftDir, p.manager())` which returns a string (the sense_loop prompt content, dry-run style with placeholder paths). So `BuildHumanLoop` does NOT write files; it returns the instance string with placeholder paths (`<draft>/loops/loop_N/prompts/think.md` etc.).\n\nBut `SaveHumanLoopPrompt` calls `GenerateHumanLoopPromptFile` which writes the actual files and returns real paths.\n\nHmm, so there's a tension. The task says handler.HumanLoop uses `builder.BuildHumanLoop` (produces method+instance). But then how does the interactive session get the sense_loop prompt file? It would need to write the instance to a file and pass it to CallCLI.\n\nWait, let me reconsider. Maybe the intended flow is:\n- `BuildHumanLoop` returns (method, instance) where instance is the full prompt content.\n- Handler writes instance to a temp file (or to loopDir/prompts/sense_loop.md).\n- Handler writes method to a temp file.\n- CallCLI(verbose, cfg, instanceFile, ModeInteractive, \"--append-system-prompt\", methodFile)\n\nBut this doesn't match \"行为不变\" (behavior unchanged) because the current flow writes think/research/exporter files too.\n\nHmm. Actually, let me step back and reconsider the scope. This is getting complicated. Let me look at whether there's a \"SaveHumanLoopPrompt\" that ALSO returns method, and whether the task wants me to keep using Save* or switch to Build*.\n\nActually, re-reading the task goal and human-loop detail, I think there might be an inconsistency in the task description itself (the plan says one thing, but the current code reality is another). Let me focus on the KEY RESULTS which are the actual acceptance criteria:\n\nKey Results:\n1. `internal/handler` 新增 `HumanLoop`/`Ctrl`/`Dream`/`Learning` 编排函数，从对应 cmd 文件迁移；`internal/cmd/{human_loop,ctrl,dream,learning}.go` 变薄\n2. 全部 8 命令 flag 行为不变；随函数迁移同步改写 `human_loop_test.go`/`learning_test.go` 等引用已迁函数的断言；另改写 `tools_test.go`（`collectExecutionData` 引用）与 `dryrun_integration_test.go`（`runLearningDryRun` 引用）；handler 以 `Options{Verbose, DryRun, JobID}` 参数接收 flag（不 import cmd）\n3. ctrl.md 模板改写为 pi JSONL 语义\n4. dream 的 4 个扫描函数迁 workspace\n5. go build + go test green; human-loop --dry-run contains sense_loop; ctrl (no --job) errors\n\nKR #1 says \"从对应 cmd 文件迁移\" (migrate from corresponding cmd files). This means: the existing orchestration logic in cmd files moves to handler, functionally equivalent. NOT rewrite to a new flow.\n\nKR #2 says \"全部 8 命令 flag 行为不变\" (all 8 command flag behaviors unchanged). \"行为不变\" (behavior unchanged).\n\nSo the KEY is: migrate the orchestration logic as-is (functionally equivalent), make cli thin. The \"env.Ensure → builder.Build → runtime\" unified orchestration in the goal is the IDEAL, but the actual per-command migration preserves existing behavior (which uses Save* functions and CallCLI).\n\nBut wait, the human-loop detail explicitly says:\n> `handler.HumanLoop`：`GetDraftDir` → `NextLoopID` → 建目录 → `builder.BuildHumanLoop`（产 method+instance）→ `env.Ensure` → `runtime.CallCLI`（交互，注入 method）→ 持久化 sessionID\n\nThis is more specific than KR #1. Hmm. But it says \"builder.BuildHumanLoop（产 method+instance）\" — which contradicts \"行为不变\" because BuildHumanLoop doesn't write files (SaveHumanLoopPrompt does).\n\nActually wait — let me reconsider. Maybe the intent is:\n- The handler should use `SaveHumanLoopPrompt` (which produces the actual prompt files), but the \"method\" part should be injected via --append-system-prompt.\n\nActually, re-reading: \"builder.BuildHumanLoop（产 method+instance）\" — maybe \"Build\" here is generic for \"the builder produces method+instance\", and the actual function is `SaveHumanLoopPrompt` which returns (mainFile, thinkFile, researchFile, exporterFile, method, err). The method is returned by SaveHumanLoopPrompt too!\n\n```go\nfunc (p *PIBuilder) SaveHumanLoopPrompt(topic, rfcDir, draftDir, loopDir string) (mainFile, thinkFile, researchFile, exporterFile, method string, err error)\n```\n\nSo SaveHumanLoopPrompt returns method. And the instance is mainFile (sense_loop prompt file). So the flow \"builder.Build...（产 method+instance 两份）→ env.Ensure → runtime.CallCLI（注入 method）→ 持久化 sessionID\" maps to:\n- Use SaveHumanLoopPrompt → get mainFile (instance file) + method.\n- env.Ensure\n- Write method to temp file, CallCLI(verbose, cfg, mainFile, ModeInteractive, \"--append-system-prompt\", methodFile)\n- persist sessionID.\n\nBut wait, \"持久化 sessionID\" — the current human-loop flow does NOT persist sessionID. It just prints \"思考记录已保存到 %s\". So this is a NEW behavior for human-loop.\n\nHmm. Actually, let me look at whether env.Ensure exists and what its signature is.\n\nLet me check the env package.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_ddtR262yX8NGcRInPrGN8127","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/env/env.go"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_VZcqlRGTsisgG4Cq0SeO3894","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/env/agents.go"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_02_49VKMACm5jA8atH2XGtD5544","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && grep -rn \"env.Ensure\\|Ensure(\" internal/env/*.go | head -30"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":4719,"output":6324,"cacheRead":91520,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":6151,"totalTokens":102563,"cost":{"input":0.0020527650000000002,"output":0.00550188,"cacheRead":0.00033176,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.007886405}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786910383390,"responseId":"c0c86419-d4a8-4cde-80da-c4c3cf2abf36","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_ddtR262yX8NGcRInPrGN8127","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// Package env 收口 rick 的 agent runtime 环境管理（env 四职责）。\n//\n// env 保证 rick 在当前机器的运行环境就绪：pi 及扩展、rick 自有定制。它是四层\n// 架构第三层「执行」的一员，对下依赖 internal/runtime 暴露的共享路径工具\n// （AgentDir/RuntimeDir/RuntimeBin/SettingsPath/AgentEnv/FileExists/EnsureAgentDir），\n// 对上被 cli（薄入口）与 handler（调度聚合）调用。\n//\n// 四职责：\n//  1. 安装/更新 pi agent（pi.go）\n//  2. 安装/更新 pi 生态扩展/插件/skill（extensions.go）\n//  3. 安装/更新 rick 自有 hook/skill/agent 定制（customizations.go）\n//  4. 提供 pi 功能点就绪 check 函数，不含 session（check.go）\n//\n// 扩展 seam：RuntimeEnv 接口 + piEnv 实现，将来新增 dsh runtime 时只实现\n// dshEnv 并注册，cli/handler 不改。\npackage env\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/runtime\"\n)\n\n// RuntimeEnv 是 env 抽象的扩展 seam（单一 runtime pi + dsh 预留）。pi 是当前\n// 唯一实现；将来 dsh 只新增 dshEnv（安装方式/扩展机制/定制落盘格式/就绪 check\n// 各自实现）并注册，cli/handler/方法层 templates 不改。\ntype RuntimeEnv interface {\n\t// Ensure 保证 runtime 就绪（安装/更新 runtime + 生态扩展 + 功能点校验）。\n\tEnsure() error\n\t// DeployCustomizations 落盘 rick 自有定制（hook/skill/agent）。\n\tDeployCustomizations() error\n\t// CheckReady 返回未就绪的功能点（空切片 = 就绪）。\n\tCheckReady() []string\n}\n\n// piEnv 是 RuntimeEnv 的 pi 实现，四职责收口于此。\ntype piEnv struct{}\n\n// NewPiEnv 构造 pi env 实现。\nfunc NewPiEnv() *piEnv { return &piEnv{} }\n\n// Ensure 委托给包级 Ensure（完整 init-pi 流程）。\nfunc (e *piEnv) Ensure() error { return Ensure() }\n\n// DeployCustomizations 委托给包级 DeployRickCustomizations。\nfunc (e *piEnv) DeployCustomizations() error { return DeployRickCustomizations() }\n\n// CheckReady 委托给包级 CheckReady。\nfunc (e *piEnv) CheckReady() []string { return CheckReady() }\n\n// Ensure 执行完整的「保证 pi 就绪」流程并返回错误。仅在 pi 完全不可用（rick 无法\n// 运行）时返回错误；缺失扩展/主题/定制仅告警，不阻断。输出与迁移前 runInitPi 逐字\n// 一致（职责 3 定制落盘静默执行，不新增输出行）。\nfunc Ensure() error {\n\t// Step 0: 前置检查 —— 仅当 rick 托管 pi runtime 尚未安装时。pi 是 Node.js\n\t// 程序（>= 22.19.0），其 npm 安装需要 node/npm 在 PATH 上。rick 不安装 node\n\t// （用户管理的环境依赖）。托管 runtime 已存在时视为环境就绪，跳过此检查。\n\tif !runtime.FileExists(runtime.RuntimeBin()) {\n\t\tif err := RequireNodeForPiInstall(); err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"❌ %v\\n\", err)\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Step 1: rick 自闭环 pi runtime 就绪（缺失则安装）。\n\tpiPath, piNewlyInstalled, err := EnsurePI()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\t// Fatal: 无 pi 则 rick 无法执行任何 agent 命令。\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"❌ pi is not available and could not be installed: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"   Install manually: npm install -g @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent\\n\")\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tver := PiVersion(piPath)\n\tfmt.Printf(\"✅ rick pi runtime ready: %s\", piPath)\n\tif ver != \"\" {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\" (v%s)\", ver)\n\t}\n\tif piNewlyInstalled {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\" (newly installed)\")\n\t}\n\tfmt.Println()\n\n\t// Step 1.5: rick 托管 agent 目录 + settings 引导（隔离配置 + hideThinkingBlock）。\n\tif err := BootstrapAgentSettings(); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"⚠️  managed agent dir: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"   rick will still run, but pi config isolation may be incomplete.\\n\")\n\t} else {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"✅ pi agent dir ready: %s (hideThinkingBlock=true)\\n\", runtime.AgentDir())\n\t}\n\n\t// Step 2: subagent 扩展注册（缺失则安装）。非致命。\n\tif err := EnsureNpmExtension(\"pi-subagents\", \"pi-subagents\"); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"⚠️  subagent extension: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"   rick works without it, but Sub Agent delegation is unavailable.\\n\")\n\t} else {\n\t\tfmt.Println(\"✅ pi subagent extension ready\")\n\t}\n\n\t// Step 3: web-access 扩展注册（缺失则安装）。非致命。\n\tif err := EnsureNpmExtension(\"pi-web-access\", \"web-access\"); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"⚠️  web-access extension: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"   rick works without it, but external web search/fetch is unavailable.\\n\")\n\t} else {\n\t\tfmt.Println(\"✅ pi web-access extension ready\")\n\t}\n\n\t// Step 4: 从托管配置清除 Tokyo Night 包。非致命。\n\tif err := PurgeTokyoNight(); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"⚠️  tokyo-night purge: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"   rick works without it; the package may still be listed.\\n\")\n\t} else {\n\t\tfmt.Println(\"✅ tokyo-night purged from managed config (theme/packages)\")\n\t}\n\n\t// Step 5: 校验所有必需扩展 + 主题已注册。\n\tmissing := VerifyExtensions()\n\tif len(missing) > 0 {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"⚠️  verification: these extensions are NOT registered: %s\\n\", strings.Join(missing, \", \"))\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"   rick may be degraded. Re-run `rick tools init-pi` or install manually.\\n\")\n\t} else {\n\t\tfmt.Println(\"✅ verification: all required extensions registered\")\n\t}\n\tif cur := CurrentTheme(); cur == \"\" {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"⚠️  verification: no theme set in settings.json\\n\")\n\t} else {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"✅ verification: theme %s active\\n\", cur)\n\t}\n\n\t// 职责 3：rick 自有定制（静默落盘，不影响 init-pi 输出基线）。\n\t_ = DeployRickCustomizations()\n\n\tfmt.Println(\"✅ pi environment ready\")\n\treturn nil\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786910449898},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01_VZcqlRGTsisgG4Cq0SeO3894","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"package env\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/prompt\"\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/runtime\"\n)\n\n// rickAgentSpec 描述一个 rick 自定义 agent：frontmatter 字段 + system prompt\n// 来源（embedded templates/skills/{name}.md，即对应源码 skill 的 wiki 内容）。\ntype rickAgentSpec struct {\n\tname           string\n\tdescription    string\n\ttools          string // 逗号分隔的 pi 工具名（与 pi-subagents tools 字段对齐）\n\tdefaultContext string\n}\n\n// rickAgents 是 rick 经 env 职责 3 注册为 pi 自定义 agent 的清单\n// （think/research/exporter）。system prompt = 对应源码 skill 的 wiki 正文。\nvar rickAgents = []rickAgentSpec{\n\t{\n\t\tname:           \"think\",\n\t\tdescription:    \"推理过程分析 + 4 维风险评估 + 启发性 3 问方法论（SENSE 的 S2 假设枚举与 EC 批判）\",\n\t\ttools:          \"read, grep, find, ls\",\n\t\tdefaultContext: \"fresh\",\n\t},\n\t{\n\t\tname:           \"research\",\n\t\tdescription:    \"尽调树 + 信源加权方法论（澄清事实模糊性到极限）\",\n\t\ttools:          \"read, grep, find, ls, bash, web_search, fetch_content\",\n\t\tdefaultContext: \"fresh\",\n\t},\n\t{\n\t\tname:           \"exporter\",\n\t\tdescription:    \"RFC 输出方法论（大纲 + 内容两阶段固化）\",\n\t\ttools:          \"read, write, bash\",\n\t\tdefaultContext: \"fresh\",\n\t},\n}\n\n// deployRickAgents 将 rick 自定义 agent 幂等写入 AgentDir()/agents/{name}.md。\n// 覆盖语义：仅当目标文件不存在，或其 frontmatter 含 rick-managed: true 标记时\n// 才写入；无标记的同名文件（用户自定义）跳过，避免覆盖用户内容。\nfunc deployRickAgents() error {\n\tagentsDir := filepath.Join(runtime.AgentDir(), \"agents\")\n\tif err := os.MkdirAll(agentsDir, 0755); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"create agents dir: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tfor _, spec := range rickAgents {\n\t\tif err := deployRickAgent(agentsDir, spec); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// deployRickAgent 写入单个 agent 文件（幂等 + rick 标记覆盖语义）。\nfunc deployRickAgent(agentsDir string, spec rickAgentSpec) error {\n\ttarget := filepath.Join(agentsDir, spec.name+\".md\")\n\tif data, err := os.ReadFile(target); err == nil {\n\t\tif !hasRickManagedMarker(string(data)) {\n\t\t\treturn nil // 无 rick 标记的用户文件，不覆盖。\n\t\t}\n\t} else if !os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"read %s: %w\", target, err)\n\t}\n\n\tbody := prompt.LoadCoreSkills([]string{spec.name})\n\tif body == \"\" {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"embedded skill %q not found for agent %q\", spec.name, spec.name)\n\t}\n\tcontent := renderRickAgentFile(spec, body)\n\tif err := os.WriteFile(target, []byte(content), 0644); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"write agent %s: %w\", spec.name, err)\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// renderRickAgentFile 渲染 agent 文件 = YAML frontmatter + system prompt 正文。\n// systemPromptMode: replace 使正文整体替换 pi 默认骨架（system prompt = wiki 内容）。\nfunc renderRickAgentFile(spec rickAgentSpec, body string) string {\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(`---\nname: %s\ndescription: %s\ntools: %s\ndefaultContext: %s\nsystemPromptMode: replace\nrick-managed: true\n---\n\n%s`, spec.name, spec.description, spec.tools, spec.defaultContext, body)\n}\n\n// hasRickManagedMarker 判断 agent 文件 frontmatter 是否含 rick-managed: true。\n// frontmatter 由首行 --- 与随后的第一个 --- 行闭合；闭合前未找到标记即视为无。\n// 解析对齐 pi 前端 frontmatter 语义：key/value 按 \":\" 分割并 trim。\nfunc hasRickManagedMarker(content string) bool {\n\tlines := strings.Split(content, \"\\n\")\n\tif len(lines) == 0 || strings.TrimSpace(lines[0]) != \"---\" {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tfor _, ln := range lines[1:] {\n\t\ttrimmed := strings.TrimSpace(ln)\n\t\tif trimmed == \"---\" {\n\t\t\treturn false\n\t\t}\n\t\tif trimmed == \"\" || strings.HasPrefix(trimmed, \"#\") {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tkv := strings.SplitN(trimmed, \":\", 2)\n\t\tif len(kv) == 2 && strings.TrimSpace(kv[0]) == \"rick-managed\" && strings.TrimSpace(kv[1]) == \"true\" {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786910449898},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_02_49VKMACm5jA8atH2XGtD5544","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"internal/env/env.go:31:\tEnsure() error\ninternal/env/env.go:45:func (e *piEnv) Ensure() error { return Ensure() }\ninternal/env/env.go:56:func Ensure() error {\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786910449898}]}
