{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, `env.Ensure()` exists and does a full init-pi flow (installs pi if needed, etc.). \n\nNow, the key question: should the new handlers (HumanLoop/Ctrl/Dream/Learning) call `env.Ensure()`?\n\nThe task goal says \"所有命令统一走「env.Ensure → builder.Build（产 method+instance 两份）→ 调用 runtime」编排\". But the current plan/doing/easy handlers (task6) do NOT call env.Ensure. They just do `workspace.New()` (which ensures dirs) + `config.LoadConfig()`.\n\nHmm, wait. Let me check if task6's plan/doing/easy handlers were supposed to call env.Ensure but didn't, OR if the \"env.Ensure\" is only for the NEW commands in task7.\n\nActually, let me re-read the task goal very carefully:\n\n> 按 spec（task2）完成 KR2.1：handler 调度聚合层覆盖剩余命令 human-loop、ctrl、dream、learning，`internal/cmd` 全部命令变薄为「路由 + 参数解析 + 调 handler」。所有命令统一走「env.Ensure → builder.Build（产 method+instance 两份）→ 调用 runtime」编排；交互命令保留 `CallCLI`（行为不变，method 经 `--append-system-prompt` 传给 `CallCLI`），`runtime.Run` 结构化签名仅 task8 的 doing 使用。\n\nSo this task (task7) covers the REMAINING commands: human-loop, ctrl, dream, learning. The \"所有命令统一走 env.Ensure → builder.Build → runtime\" is the GOAL.\n\nBut wait, task6 already did plan/doing/easy. Did task6 use env.Ensure? Looking at handler/plan.go and handler/doing.go and handler/easy.go, they do NOT call env.Ensure.\n\nSo either:\n(a) task6 was incomplete (didn't use env.Ensure), and task7 should use env.Ensure for the new 4 commands but NOT touch the existing 3 (to avoid regression), OR\n(b) task7 should ALSO retroactively add env.Ensure to plan/doing/easy, OR\n(c) \"env.Ensure\" in the goal is aspirational and the actual per-command detail only specifies env.Ensure for human-loop.\n\nLooking at the per-command details:\n- human-loop: \"`handler.HumanLoop`：`GetDraftDir` → `NextLoopID` → 建目录 → `builder.BuildHumanLoop`（产 method+instance）→ `env.Ensure` → `runtime.CallCLI`（交互，注入 method）→ 持久化 sessionID\"\n- ctrl: \"cli 保留 `NewCtrlCmd`（`--job` 必传校验 + 调 handler）；迁出 `runCtrl`/`runCtrlDryRun` → `handler.Ctrl`/`handler.CtrlDryRun`\" — no env.Ensure mention.\n- dream: \"迁出 `dreamWorkflow`→`handler.Dream`、`runDreamDryRun`→`handler.DreamDryRun`、... 4 个扫描函数\" — no env.Ensure mention.\n- learning: \"迁出 `executeLearningWorkflow`→`handler.Learning`、`runLearningDryRun`→`handler.LearningDryRun`、`collectExecutionData`、`callAgentForAnalysis`、`buildLearningPrompt`\" — no env.Ensure mention.\n\nSo only human-loop explicitly mentions env.Ensure. The others just say \"migrate from cmd file\".\n\nHmm. But the goal says \"所有命令统一走 env.Ensure\". This is confusing.\n\nLet me think about what's SAFE and CORRECT for the tests:\n\nThe critical acceptance criteria are:\n1. Build + tests green\n2. Specific behaviors (human-loop dry-run contains sense_loop, ctrl no-job error, dream scan, learning tasks.json not found, ctrl doing dir not found)\n\nAdding env.Ensure to a command would trigger pi installation/checking, which:\n- In tests, could hang or fail (since tests use mock pi via cfg.PiPath, but env.Ensure checks RuntimeBin etc.)\n- Would change behavior (prints \"✅ rick pi runtime ready\" etc.)\n\nActually, env.Ensure is potentially DANGEROUS in tests because it tries to install pi if not available, runs npm commands, etc. If I add env.Ensure to human-loop, the human-loop tests would try to run env.Ensure which would check for node/npm, try to install pi, etc.\n\nWait, but the human-loop tests use `os.Chdir(workDir)` with a mock pi and a config.json with `pi_path`. env.Ensure would:\n1. Check RuntimeBin() — `~/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/.bin/pi` — if it exists (it does on this machine), skip node check.\n2. EnsurePI() — check pi path... this could install or just verify.\n3. BootstrapAgentSettings() — write settings.json to AgentDir() (real ~/.rick/pi/agent).\n4. etc.\n\nThis would be a REAL side effect on the actual machine, and could be slow. That's bad for tests.\n\nHmm wait, but actually the human-loop tests set `HOME` to temp dir in `TestHumanLoopCreatesDraftDirs` and `TestHumanLoopCmdWithMockClaude`. So `AgentDir()` = `$HOME/.rick/pi/agent` = temp. So env.Ensure would operate on temp dir. But it would still try to install pi (npm install) which is slow and may fail in the test environment.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. Let me check what the actual current behavior is and whether env.Ensure is called anywhere currently.\n\nLet me grep for env.Ensure usage.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_BVsaLRmkPFKJh4eAXdRu3779","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && grep -rn \"env\\.\\|internal/env\\|env.Ensure\\|env.NewPiEnv\" internal/cmd/*.go internal/handler/*.go | head -40"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_TiJ8gRcMdixXe1VBOzvE0806","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && grep -rn \"env\\.\" internal/cmd/*.go | head -40"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":2904,"output":1401,"cacheRead":102528,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1245,"totalTokens":106833,"cost":{"input":0.0012632400000000001,"output":0.0012188700000000002,"cacheRead":0.000371664,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.002853774}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786910449900,"responseId":"c8196e83-6c65-4ce0-a3aa-92a338c7ed50","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_BVsaLRmkPFKJh4eAXdRu3779","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"internal/cmd/tools_init_pi.go:9:\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/env\"\ninternal/cmd/tools_init_pi.go:15:// delegated to internal/env (env 四职责收口) — this command is a thin Cobra\ninternal/cmd/tools_init_pi.go:40:\t\t\tif err := env.Ensure(); err != nil {\ninternal/cmd/tools_theme.go:13:\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/env\"\ninternal/cmd/tools_theme.go:24:// The embedded theme JSON lives in internal/env/themes/ and is written by\ninternal/cmd/t