ace. So workspace → executor is fine (no cycle).\n\nBut wait, is it clean for workspace (L4 infra) to import executor (which is on the delete list)? The task says \"discoverCompletedJobs 依赖的 executor.LoadTasksJSON... 迁 workspace（极薄读取器，task8 显式落地）\". So in task7, workspace imports executor temporarily; task8 moves the thin reader into workspace.\n\nHmm, actually, re-reading once more: \"tasks.json 极薄读取器类型定义在 task8 落地\" — the thin reader TYPE DEFINITION lands in task8. So in task7, I do NOT define the thin reader in workspace; I keep using executor.LoadTasksJSON. But then workspace imports executor.\n\nWait, but actually, maybe I should reconsider whether the scan functions should go in workspace OR handler. Let me re-read KR #4:\n\n> 4. **dream 的 4 个扫描函数**（`selectPendingJobs`/`getDreamProcessedJobs`/`discoverCompletedJobs`/`jobNumber`）迁 workspace（本 task 迁编排，tasks.json 极薄读取器类型定义在 task8 落地）\n\n\"迁 workspace\" = migrate to workspace. So they go in workspace.\n\nSo workspace will import executor in task7. That's the plan. In task8, the thin reader (LoadTasksJSON) will be moved into workspace, and workspace will stop importing executor.\n\nActually, wait — there might be a subtlety. Let me check: does `executor` package have a `LoadDebugContext` function that learning also needs? Let me check executor/debug_dir.go.\n\nActually, for the learning command, `collectExecutionData` uses:\n- `executor.LoadDebugContext(doingDir)`\n- `executor.LoadTasksJSON(tasksJSONPath)`\n- `tasksJSON.Tasks` (the field directly)\n\nAnd the task says for learning:\n> ### learning（依赖 executor + parser + actpath，task8 一并闭环）\n> - 依赖闭环（task8）：`executor.LoadTasksJSON`/`TasksJSON`/`TaskState` + `executor.LoadDebugContext` + `parser.ExtractBugFrontmatter` → 迁 workspace/prompt 极薄实现\n\nSo learning's executor/parser dependencies are also \"task8 一并闭环\" (closed in task8). So in task7, learning handler can still import executor (for LoadTasksJSON/LoadDebugContext) and parser (ExtractBugFrontmatter, if used).