yRun)\n\nLet me now check whether there's a potential circular import issue with handler importing workspace and workspace importing executor... handler already imports workspace and executor. So handler → workspace → executor, and handler → executor. No cycle.\n\nBut wait — workspace importing executor: does executor import workspace? No (checked earlier: executor imports actpath, agent, parser, prompt). So workspace → executor is fine.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me reconsider whether to put the 4 scan functions in workspace or somewhere else. The concern: workspace is \"L4 基础设施\" (path resolution). Putting job-scanning logic (which reads tasks.json) there is a bit odd, but the task explicitly says \"迁 workspace\".\n\nLet me also reconsider: is there any issue with `workspace` package having a function that imports `executor`? The `executor` package is on the delete list (task8). After task8, workspace's `discoverCompletedJobs` will use workspace's own thin reader. So the temporary import is fine.\n\nActually, wait — let me reconsider. There might be a subtle issue: if I put `DiscoverCompletedJobs` in workspace and it imports executor, and in task8 the thin reader lands in workspace, then workspace would have BOTH the thin reader AND import executor (until task8 removes it). That's fine for task7.\n\nAlternatively, I could avoid the executor import entirely by writing a minimal inline reader in workspace now. But the task says \"极薄读取器类型定义在 task8 落地\" (thin reader type lands in task8), implying I should NOT create it now. So I'll import executor in workspace.\n\nHmm, but actually, wait. Let me reconsider. There's a cleaner interpretation: maybe the scan functions should go into a NEW file in workspace that just uses `executor.LoadTasksJSON`. Let me verify executor.LoadTasksJSON and TasksJSON.GetAllTasks and TaskState.Status are all exported (they are, from tasks_json.go). And `discoverCompletedJobs` uses:\n- `executor.LoadTasksJSON(f)` → *TasksJSON\n- `tj.GetAllTasks()` → []TaskState\n- `t.Status` field access\n\nAll exported. Good.\n\nLet me now write all the files.\n\nFirst, let me write the workspace dream scan functions.\n\nActually, let me reconsider naming. The task says \"迁 workspace\". The functions currently are unexported in cmd: `selectPendingJobs`, `getDreamProcessedJobs`, `discoverCompletedJobs`, `jobNumber`. When migrating to workspace (a different package), they need to be EXPORTED (since handler will call them): `SelectPendingJobs`, `GetDreamProcessedJobs`, `DiscoverCompletedJobs`, `JobNumber`.\n\nLet me write them.\n\nNow, let me also decide: should I write a workspace test for these? The task's test method says \"dream 只列「完成且未 dream」的 job（排除未完成/已 dream，按 job 号升序截断）\". This is tested via the CLI (`dream --dry-run`). There might not be a Go unit test for the scan functions currently (they're in cmd/dream.go with no dream_test.go). Let me check if there's a dream test.\n\nFrom the grep earlier, there's no dream_test.go. So no existing Go test for the scan functions. The scan filtering is tested via the CLI test method (manually or integration). \n\nBut to be safe and thorough, I could add a workspace test for the scan functions. This would strengthen the implementation. But it's optional. Let me add a lightweight test to verify the scan filtering works (completed + not dreamed + sorted + truncated). This aligns with the \"dream 扫描过滤\" acceptance criterion.\n\nActually, let me focus on the required tests first, and add a workspace scan test as a bonus (it helps validate my implementation and matches the \"dream 扫描过滤\" boundary test).\n\nLet me now write everything.\n\nLet me start with the workspace dream scan file.\n\nActually, one more check: the `discoverCompletedJobs` function extracts job ID via `filepath.Base(filepath.Dir(filepath.Dir(f)))`. For `f = .rick/jobs/job_5/doing/tasks.json`, Dir = .rick/jobs/job_5/doing, Dir again = .rick/jobs/job_5, Base = job_5. Correct.\n\nNow let me write the code. I'll create files in order.\n\nLet me write `internal/workspace/dream.go`:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a complete understanding. Let me start implementing. First, the workspace dream scan functions:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_QFLvCYLKRBImf5HtqaLb3758","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/workspace/dream.go","content":"package workspace\n\nimport (\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strconv\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/executor\"\n)\n\n// SelectPendingJobs returns up to jobNum completed jobs not yet processed by\n// dream (migrated from cmd.selectPendingJobs). The scan/filtering stays in Go:\n// it is the deterministic input filter that decides which jobs dream should\n// process.\n//\n// NOTE: discoverCompletedJobs still reads tasks.json through executor's thin\n// LoadTasksJSON reader today; the reader type itself is moved into workspace\n// explicitly in task8 (做薄 cutover), after which this import is dropped.\nfunc SelectPendingJobs(rickDir string, jobNum int) []string {\n\tcompleted := DiscoverCompletedJobs(rickDir)\n\tprocessed := GetDreamProcessedJobs(rickDir)\n\n\tvar pending []string\n\tfor _, id := range completed {\n\t\tif !processed[id] {\n\t\t\tpending = append(pending, id)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tif len(pending) > jobNum {\n\t\tpending = pending[:jobNum]\n\t}\n\treturn pending\n}\n\n// GetDreamProcessedJobs returns the set of job IDs that already have a\n// dream_run_{job_id}_log.md file in .rick/dream/ (migrated from\n// cmd.getDreamProcessedJobs).\nfunc GetDreamProcessedJobs(rickDir string) map[string]bool {\n\tprocessed := make(map[string]bool)\n\tdreamDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, DreamDirName)\n\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(dreamDir)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn processed\n\t}\n\tfor _, e := range entries {\n\t\tif e.IsDir() {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tname := e.Name()\n\t\t// Expected format: dream_run_job_N_log.md\n\t\tif !strings.HasPrefix(name, \"dream_run_\") || !strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_log.md\") {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tjobID := strings.TrimPrefix(name, \"dream_run_\")\n\t\tjobID = strings.TrimSuffix(jobID, \"_log.md\")\n\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(jobID, \"job_\") {\n\t\t\tprocessed[jobID] = true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn processed\n}\n\n// DiscoverCompletedJobs scans .rick/jobs/*/doing/tasks.json and returns jobs\n// where all tasks have status \"success\", sorted by job number ascending\n// (migrated from cmd.discoverCompletedJobs).\nfunc DiscoverCompletedJobs(rickDir string) []string {\n\tpattern := filepath.Join(rickDir, JobsDirName, \"job_*\", DoingDirName, \"tasks.json\")\n\tfiles, err := filepath.Glob(pattern)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\n\tvar completed []string\n\tfor _, f := range files {\n\t\ttj, err := executor.LoadTasksJSON(f)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\ttasks := tj.GetAllTasks()\n\t\tif len(tasks) == 0 {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tallDone := true\n\t\tfor _, t := range tasks {\n\t\t\tif t.Status != \"success\" {\n\t\t\t\tallDone = false\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif allDone {\n\t\t\t// Extract job ID from path: .rick/jobs/job_N/doing/tasks.json\n\t\t\tjobID := filepath.Base(filepath.Dir(filepath.Dir(f)))\n\t\t\tcompleted = append(completed, jobID)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tsort.Slice(completed, func(i, j int) bool {\n\t\treturn JobNumber(completed[i]) < JobNumber(completed[j])\n\t})\n\treturn completed\n}\n\n// JobNumber extracts the numeric part from \"job_N\" (migrated from\n// cmd.jobNumber). Returns 0 for malformed IDs.\nfunc JobNumber(jobID string) int {\n\tn, _ := strconv.Atoi(strings.TrimPrefix(jobID, \"job_\"))\n\treturn n\n}\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1043,"output":3403,"cacheRead":130560,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":2439,"totalTokens":135006,"cost":{"input":0.000453705,"output":0.0029606100000000002,"cacheRead":0.00047328,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0038875