n\nThe cleanest solution: define a minimal tasks.json reader in workspace (a thin struct with just Status field), and use it in DiscoverCompletedJobs. This is actually what task8 would do, but I need it now to avoid the cycle.\n\nLet me write a minimal reader in workspace/dream.go:\n\n```go\n// thin tasks.json reader (the explicit landing is task8; defined here now to\n// avoid the workspace→executor→prompt→workspace import cycle)\ntype taskStateJSON struct {\n    TaskID string `json:\"task_id\"`\n    Status string `json:\"status\"`\n}\n\ntype tasksJSON struct {\n    Tasks []taskStateJSON `json:\"tasks\"`\n}\n\nfunc loadTasksJSON(path string) (*tasksJSON, error) {\n    data, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n    if err != nil {\n        return nil, err\n    }\n    var tj tasksJSON\n    if err := json.Unmarshal(data, &tj); err != nil {\n        return nil, err\n    }\n    return &tj, nil\n}\n```\n\nThis is a minimal thin reader. It only reads Status. This matches the intent (\"极薄读取器\").\n\nThen `DiscoverCompletedJobs` uses this instead of `executor.LoadTasksJSON`:\n```go\ntj, err := loadTasksJSON(f)\nif err != nil { continue }\ntasks := tj.Tasks\nif len(tasks) == 0 { continue }\nallDone := true\nfor _, t := range tasks {\n    if t.Status != \"success\" { allDone = false; break }\n}\n...\n```\n\nThis breaks the cycle and is actually cleaner (workspace no longer imports executor).\n\nWait, but the task says \"discoverCompletedJobs 依赖的 executor.LoadTasksJSON + TasksJSON.GetAllTasks() + TaskState.Status 迁 workspace（极薄读取器，task8 显式落地）\". So the intent IS that workspace has its own thin reader. The \"task8 显式落地\" is about the FORMAL type landing, but since I'm migrating the scan functions now and they need the reader, I'll inline a minimal reader now. This is consistent with the intent and avoids the cycle.\n\nActually, re-reading even more carefully: \"本 task 迁编排，tasks.json 极薄读取器类型定义在 task8 落地\". This says \"this task migrates the orchestration; the tasks.json thin reader TYPE DEFINITION lands in task8\". \n\nHmm, so the intent is:\n- task7: migrate scan functions (orchestration) to workspace.\n- task8: define the thin reader type in workspace.\n\nBut this creates a cycle in task7 (workspace imports executor). Unless... the intent is that in task7, the scan functions are in workspace but STILL use executor, and the cycle is somehow avoided.\n\nWait, let me re-examine the cycle. Is prompt → workspace actually a hard import? Let me check what prompt/doing_prompt.go imports from workspace.\n\nLet me check the exact import.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_MIvhWwv3U4gvxofb3QEw1543","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && grep -rn \"sunquan/rick/internal\" internal/prompt/*.go | grep -v \"_test\" | sort -u && echo \"=== which prompt files import workspace ===\" && grep -rln \"internal/workspace\" internal/prompt/*.go"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":213,"output":1139,"cacheRead":141440,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1024,"totalTokens":142792,"cost":{"input":0.000092655,"output":0.0009909300000000001,"cacheRead":0.00051272,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0015963050000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786910837393,"responseId":"fb1a22de-abad-4dd8-9092-5b57297246bd","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_MIvhWwv3U4gvxofb3QEw1543","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"internal/prompt/context.go:9:\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/parser\"\ninternal/prompt/context_helpers.go:10:\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/parser\"\ninternal/prompt/doing_prompt.go:10:\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/workspace\"\ninternal/prompt/doing_prompt.go:9:\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/parser\"\ninternal/prompt/easy_prompt.go:10:\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/parser\"\n=== which prompt files import workspace ===\ninternal/prompt/doing_prompt.go\n"}]