{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The handler and workspace packages compile and pass tests already (since I moved the functions there, but the cmd tests still reference the old functions).\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Update `internal/cmd/learning_test.go` — remove migrated tests.\n2. Update `internal/cmd/tools_test.go` — remove collectExecutionData tests.\n3. Update `internal/cmd/dryrun_integration_test.go` — runLearningDryRun → handler.LearningDryRun.\n4. Create `internal/handler/learning_test.go` with migrated tests.\n5. Update `internal/cmd/human_loop_test.go` — the dry-run capture issue.\n\nLet me handle the learning_test.go first. I'll rewrite it to keep only TestLearningTemplateHasDraftDir.\n\nActually, let me re-examine learning_test.go's content to see exactly what to keep and remove.\n\nCurrent learning_test.go:\n1. `TestBuildLearningPrompt` — uses ExecutionData, buildLearningPrompt → MOVE to handler\n2. `TestExecutionDataStruct` — uses ExecutionData → MOVE to handler\n3. `TestExecuteLearningWorkflow_NoDoingDir` — uses executeLearningWorkflow → MOVE to handler (rename to Learning)\n4. `TestLearningTemplateHasDraftDir` — uses prompt package → KEEP in cmd\n5. `TestBuildLearningPromptInjectsDraftDir` — uses ExecutionData, buildLearningPrompt → MOVE to handler\n6. `TestExecuteLearningWorkflow_WithMockPi` — uses executeLearningWorkflow → MOVE to handler (rename to Learning)\n\nSo learning_test.go will keep only TestLearningTemplateHasDraftDir.\n\nLet me rewrite learning_test.go to keep only the template test.\n\nThen create handler/learning_test.go with the migrated tests.\n\nLet me first write the handler/learning_test.go. The migrated tests need:\n- imports: encoding/json, fmt, os, path/filepath, strings, testing, executor, prompt\n\nLet me write it based on the original tests but adapted:\n- `TestBuildLearningPrompt` → same, but in handler package (uses ExecutionData, buildLearningPrompt directly).\n- `TestExecutionDataStruct` → same.\n- `TestLearning_NoDoingDir` (was TestExecuteLearningWorkflow_NoDoingDir) → calls `Learning(\"job_test\", Options{})`.\n- `TestLearningTemplateHasDraftDir` → stays in cmd (uses prompt package). Actually, I could keep it in handler too, but it's about the template. I'll keep it in cmd to minimize changes. Actually wait, it doesn't reference any migrated function, so it can stay in cmd.\n- `TestBuildLearningPromptInjectsDraftDir` → same, uses ExecutionData + buildLearningPrompt.\n- `TestLearning_WithMockPi` (was TestExecuteLearningWorkflow_WithMockPi) → calls `Learning(\"job_test\", Options{})`.\n- `TestCollectExecutionData_NoDoingDir` (from tools_test.go) → uses collectExecutionData.\n- `TestCollectExecutionData_WithData` → uses collectExecutionData + a makeTasksJSON helper.\n- `TestCollectExecutionData_NoDebugMD` → uses collectExecutionData + makeTasksJSON.\n\nFor makeTasksJSON, I need a helper in handler test. Let me write a helper `writeTasksJSON` in handler/learning_test.go.\n\nActually, the original `makeTasksJSON` in tools_test.go takes `[]executor.TaskState` and marshals to tasks.json. Let me replicate a similar helper.\n\nLet me write the handler learning_test.go now.\n\nFor the mock pi test (TestLearning_WithMockPi), the original uses:\n- mock pi script\n- chdir to temp\n- create doing dir with tasks.json + debug.md\n- set PATH to include mock dir\n- isolate HOME + config.json with pi_path\n- call executeLearningWorkflow(\"job_test\")\n\nI'll adapt to `Learning(\"job_test\", Options{})`.\n\nLet me write the full handler/learning_test.go.\n\nActually, let me be careful about the `t.Setenv` vs `os.Setenv` + defer pattern. The original learning_test.go uses `t.Setenv(\"HOME\", home)` in TestExecuteLearningWorkflow_WithMockPi and `os.Setenv(\"PATH\", ...)` with defer. I'll preserve these.\n\nLet me write it now."}}
