{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The only \"internal/cmd\" references in handler are in comments (options.go). No actual import. Good.\n\nNow let me do a final comprehensive verification and then summarize.\n\nActually, let me verify the full picture once more with a clean final run of the exact required test command plus the CLI behavior checks, all in one go, to produce a clean final report.\n\nActually, I've already verified everything. Let me just do a final confirmation run and then write the summary.\n\nLet me confirm:\n1. go build -o bin/rick ./cmd/rick ✓ (done)\n2. go test ./internal/cmd/... ./internal/handler/... -timeout 60s ✓ (done)\n3. human-loop --dry-run contains sense_loop ✓ (4 occurrences)\n4. dream --dry-run scan filtering ✓\n5. ctrl no --job error ✓\n6. learning tasks.json not found ✓\n7. ctrl doing dir not found ✓\n8. doing_check ✓\n\nAll done. Let me write a concise summary.\n\nActually, wait — I should double check one thing about the tasks.json. When I did `json.dump(..., ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)`, the previous tasks.json used indent 2 too (based on my initial read it showed 2-space indent). Let me verify the tasks.json is still valid and doing_check still passes (already ran doing_check → passed, so it's valid).\n\nLet me also make sure the `bin/rick` committed is actually my freshly-built one. I ran `go build -o bin/rick ./cmd/rick` before the CLI checks, and then committed `bin/rick` with -f. So yes.\n\nEverything is complete. Let me write the final summary.\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether there's anything I missed from the task requirements:\n\nRe-reading the task's \"关键结果\":\n1. ✓ handler HumanLoop/Ctrl/Dream/Learning + cmd thin\n2. ✓ flag behaviors + tests\n3. ✓ ctrl.md pi JSONL (I did the NDJSON→pi JSONL rewrite; the \"act-path 引用改 runtime trace\" part — I kept act-path.md but reworded to \"行为轨迹摘要（runtime trace）\". This is a reasonable interpretation.)\n4. ✓ dream scan