he set of job IDs that already have a\n// dream_run_{job_id}_log.md file in .rick/dream/. Exported wrapper for\n// getDreamProcessedJobs.\nfunc GetDreamProcessedJobs(rickDir string) map[string]bool {\n\treturn getDreamProcessedJobs(rickDir)\n}\n\nfunc getDreamProcessedJobs(rickDir string) map[string]bool {\n\t...\n}\n\nfunc DiscoverCompletedJobs(rickDir string) []string {\n\treturn discoverCompletedJobs(rickDir)\n}\n\nfunc discoverCompletedJobs(rickDir string) []string {\n\t...\n}\n\nfunc JobNumber(jobID string) int {\n\treturn jobNumber(jobID)\n}\n\nfunc jobNumber(jobID string) int {\n\tn, _ := strconv.Atoi(strings.TrimPrefix(jobID, \"job_\"))\n\treturn n\n}\n```\n\nThis is clean. Let me implement it.\n\nWait, but I should double check: does the test require the lowercase function to be a \"real\" function or just any match? It's just a regex match on `func selectPendingJobs(`. So any `func selectPendingJobs(` will match. But I want real implementations to be lowercase (not the wrapper), which is fine.\n\nActually, I realize I could simplify: just have lowercase be the implementation, and exported wrappers delegate. That's what I'll do.\n\nLet me also verify there are no other issues. Let me run the test7.py first to see the current full state, then make my fix.\n\nActually, the feedback only showed the workspace issue. But let me verify by running the test7.py myself. But first, let me make sure I understand: the previous commit d184e12 and b46de75 are already done. So most of the work is done. I just need to fix the workspace naming issue.\n\nLet me run the test to confirm current state.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me run the test script to confirm the current failure state."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_nHQK8JZzFdenonH6VYeK4006","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && python3 .rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tests/task7.py 2>&1 | tail -5"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek